{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1110,
    "dDurationMs": 4850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Light is a wave, and as it travels it does\nits \"waving\" along a certain direction - its"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5960,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "polarization. Polarization, among other things,\nheavily influences the way light bounces and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11400,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scatters - that's why horizontally polarized\nlight reflects off of a lake or car windshield,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16500,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which in turn is why sunglasses with a vertical\npolarizing filter can block that light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21440,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in the hot plasma of the baby universe,\nlight was bouncing off of electrons left and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26520,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "right - until the plasma cooled enough to\nbecome transparent so the light could start"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30380,
    "dDurationMs": 4949,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "traveling through space. But before heading\nout on its 13+ billion year journey, this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35329,
    "dDurationMs": 5181,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "light bounced one last time off of the plasma,\nand the direction each photon went was influenced"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40510,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by how its polarization interacted with the\nprecise temperature, density and motion of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44980,
    "dDurationMs": 1030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the plasma."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46010,
    "dDurationMs": 4819,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if we measure the polarization of light\ncoming from this cosmic background radiation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50829,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it can tell us about the big bang. The details\nare complicated, but roughly speaking, clumps"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55989,
    "dDurationMs": 5590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the plasma of the early universe created\npolarization aligned along or across the direction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61579,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from hot to cold, while jiggles created polarization\nat 45° angles to the hot-cold direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69110,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And by jiggles I mean the stretching and squeezing\nof space due to gravitational waves passing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73030,
    "dDurationMs": 760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73790,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Anyway, starting with the results from the\nBICEP telescope at the South Pole, we see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78030,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that while a majority of the polarization\ncame from clumps in the early universe, about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82190,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "15% of it seems to come from jiggles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85150,
    "dDurationMs": 4969,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And these jiggles are a big deal - they were\ncaused just fractions of fractions of a second"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90119,
    "dDurationMs": 5161,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into the life of the universe by quantum fluctuations\nof the gravitational field, so not only does"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95280,
    "dDurationMs": 4390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their discovery mark the first confirmation\nthat gravity is indeed a quantum mechanical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99670,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "phenomenon, but it also opens the door for\nus to look 380,000 years farther back than"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104570,
    "dDurationMs": 4729,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ever before, into the very birth of our cosmos."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109299,
    "dDurationMs": 4051,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Congrats to the BICEP collaboration! - assuming\nof course, that their results are confirmed"
    } ]
  } ]
}
